      <h1>LLM Providers</h1>
      <p>The platform supports 4 LLM providers with automatic fallback.</p>

      <table class="docs-table">
        <tr><th>Provider</th><th>Models</th><th>Config</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Ollama (Local)</td><td>llama3, mistral, phi3</td><td><code>OLLAMA_HOST</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Azure OpenAI</td><td>GPT-4o, GPT-4, GPT-3.5</td><td><code>AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY</code>, <code>AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>OpenAI</td><td>GPT-4o, GPT-4, GPT-3.5</td><td><code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Azure AI Foundry</td><td>Custom deployments</td><td><code>AZURE_AI_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT</code>, <code>AZURE_AI_FOUNDRY_KEY</code></td></tr>
      </table>

      <div class="docs-callout tip">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Ollama works out of the box with no API keys. For cloud providers, set the appropriate environment variables in your <code>.env</code> file.
      </div>

      <h2>Provider Selection</h2>
      <p>When running an agent, you can select the provider/model from the dropdown. The platform will attempt to use the selected provider and fall back to others if unavailable.</p>
